            <ArticleTitle>Intensive statin therapy in coronary artery disease: is lower cholesterol better and safe?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-39</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2217/14796678.5.2.129</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary- and secondary-prevention trials involving subjects with or at risk for coronary artery disease have previously demonstrated a beneficial effect of conventional-dose statin therapy. Recent trials of high-dose statin therapy in subjects with stable coronary disease or acute coronary syndromes have yielded conflicting results. The aim of this narrative article is to provide a critical and up-to-date summary of the findings of clinical trials of intensive statin therapy, including a brief overview of the safety and efficacy of such treatments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
